<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78048" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραιθύσσω</span></b> , poet. aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αίθυξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).73
				</span></i>
			:—<i>move</i> or <i>stir in passing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρα πτερύγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.204
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θόρυβον π.</span>
			<i>raise</i> a shout <i>in applause</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>whizz past</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαίφεα πτερύγεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.1253
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., of
			words, <i>fall by chance from</i> a person's lips, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τι καὶ φλαῦρον π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.87
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
